(a large budget across many seeds should exercise nesting: the generated
 text must contain at least one nested construct and one buffer)
(Plain layout, because the nesting marker below is four spaces and this
 test is asking about CONTENT - whether the generator nests at all - not
 about how that content is laid out. Under the random layout an indent is
 drawn, so four spaces in a row is a coin toss and this would be a flaky
 test of the wrong thing. 270_layout is where layout is gated, and it
 proves the two modes differ in whitespace alone.)
'gen set layout' of "plain".
'gen program' of 7 and 40.
a text called 'the generated program' is 'gen text'.
a text called 'the buffer marker' is "a buffer called".
a text called 'the nesting marker' is "    ".
a boolean called 'a buffer appears' is 'gen text contains' of 'the buffer marker'.
a boolean called 'nesting appears' is 'gen text contains' of 'the nesting marker'.
Print "has buffer: {'a buffer appears'}".
Print "has nesting: {'nesting appears'}".
